Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 19:13:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?P51:=20SCH=5FSHEET=5FLIST::AnnotatePowerSymbols?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20fix=20dead-code=20&&=20vs=20||=20guard?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Line was 'curr_ref.Last() < 0 && curr_ref.Last() > 9' — no character
can be simultaneously less than '0' and greater than '9', so the
'skip unannotated refs' fast-path never triggered.

Behaviour is unchanged today: an unannotated ref has no trailing
digits to strip, so the loop that runs after the dead-code guard is
a no-op on those refs. But the guard was intended to save that
work AND clarify intent — the || form does both.

Same shape as P34 (courtyard-constraint typo): harmless-today
copy/paste bug that would silently break if the surrounding logic
ever tightened up.
---
 eeschema/sch_sheet_path.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/eeschema/sch_sheet_path.cpp b/eeschema/sch_sheet_path.cpp
index fb669c5e..138ba689 100644
--- a/eeschema/sch_sheet_path.cpp
+++ b/eeschema/sch_sheet_path.cpp
@@ -1422,8 +1422,18 @@ void SCH_SHEET_LIST::AnnotatePowerSymbols()
             continue;
         }
 
-        // Possible duplicate, if the ref ends by a number:
-        if( curr_ref.Last() < '0' && curr_ref.Last() > '9' )
+        // Possible duplicate, if the ref ends by a number.
+        //
+        // Bug fix: this used to read
+        //     curr_ref.Last() < '0' && curr_ref.Last() > '9'
+        // which is impossible (a char cannot be both < '0' and > '9')
+        // so the guard was dead code and the intended "skip
+        // unannotated refs" fast-path never triggered. The digit-strip
+        // loop below then ran on the un-annotated ref, but because
+        // there were no trailing digits to strip it was a functional
+        // no-op — so the behaviour is unchanged, only the intent is
+        // now correctly expressed. The right operator is ||.
+        if( curr_ref.Last() < '0' || curr_ref.Last() > '9' )
             continue;   // not annotated
 
         // Duplicate: clear annotation by removing the number ending the ref
